# Loaded only by `vite build` (mode=production); overrides .env, which holds the
# localhost value used by `npm run dev`.
#
# A RELATIVE url on purpose. On DigitalOcean App Platform the static site and
# the API service sit behind one domain, so the browser calls the same origin it
# was served from. That means:
#   - no CORS preflight and no FRONTEND_ORIGIN to keep in sync
#   - the session cookie is first-party, so sameSite=lax just works
#   - the same build artifact works on any domain without rebuilding
#
# This must match the API service's HTTP route in the App Platform spec, and
# that route needs preserve_path_prefix=true so the /api prefix still reaches
# Express (which mounts everything under BASE_PATH=/api).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
